  "query_preview": "..\nSatellite imagery depicts isolated thunderstorms and locally heavy \nshowers in a north-to-south oriented axis along the Marianas. The \nconvective activity began in the far northern Marianas this morning \nand has backfilled southward along a train of showers as the day \nprogressed. A subtropical ridge has set up to the northeast, \nadvecting drier air which will push off the convection to the west \nover the western and southern coastal waters of Tinian and Saipan in \nthe early evening. As for Rota and Guam, the convective activity is \nnot expected to subside until after midnight when the drier air \ncompletely envelops the region, bringing partly cloudy skies and \nisolated showers for the Marianas early Friday morning through Friday\nnight. The trades are expected to increase as the ridge continues to\nintensify, so breezy winds and scattered showers are a possibility \naround early next week.",
